    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Kinroot v4: how this pipeline works\n1. Website at localhost:8501 uploads PDF and triggers POST /webhook/kinroot-source.\n2. This canvas searches TikTok, Pinterest, Douyin (Apify) and YouTube (official API).\n3. Normalized candidates flow back to the local website API at kinroot-api:8502.\n4. **The website**, not these search nodes, performs Groq metadata ranking and strict **visual >=70/100** qualification on accessible permitted direct-media files.\n5. Verified-license direct-media candidates may be downloaded, analyzed and trimmed automatically; ordinary social links remain metadata candidates unless an authorized acquisition source exists.\n6. Review site shows 1080p trimmed files (3-second core + 1-second handles) for Approve/Reject. Reject deletes temporary source/preview, approve retains export.\n7. Credentials are intentionally omitted from the JSON. Reconnect Apify Bearer Auth on its 3 search nodes and Google Query Auth (name `key`) on YouTube. Publish the workflow.\n**Important:** Scraper Actors may cost credits. Do not assume metadata proves visual match, actual source resolution, or commercial reuse rights. Facebook is not connected to a general public keyword-search API.\n",
        "height": 485,
        "width": 690,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "bd5c4def-320e-480f-934e-57068a6f1bb0",
      "name": "START HERE — IMPORTANT",
